speechtext:
Mr. JEAN-FRANCOIS POULIOT (Temis-couata) moved:
That, in the opinion of this house, chapter 2 of 23-24 George V (1933) should be repealed;
That the trade agreement entered into between representatives of His Majesty's government in Canada and of His Majesty's government in the United Kingdom, copy of which is set forth in the schedule of the above mentioned act, should be revoked;
And that chapter 13 of 20-21 George V (1930), an act to amend the customs tariff, should be substituted thereto.
Hon. CHARLES A. DUNNING (Minister of Finance): Mr. Speaker, much as I appreciate the compliment contained in the last paragraph of the motion, I think I must call your attention to the fact that this resolution is entirely out of order.
[Mr. Dubois.3
